0.300 0.100 0.100 rg
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 42.00 108.50 Td (1. NO RECYCLE BIN: 'rm' deletes immediately at filesystem level. There is no undo and no trash folder in terminal!) Tj ET
0.300 0.100 0.100 rg
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 42.00 99.50 Td (2. NEVER RUN 'rm -rf /*': Forcefully obliterates every mounted file, configuration, and kernel node on the entire system.) Tj ET
0.300 0.100 0.100 rg
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 42.00 90.50 Td (3. QUOTE PATHS WITH SPACES: 'rm my notes.txt' deletes TWO files: 'my' and 'notes.txt'! Always write 'rm "my notes.txt"'!) Tj ET
0.300 0.100 0.100 rg
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 42.00 81.50 Td (4. BEWARE TAB OVERWRITE: Accidental Tab completion on mv or cp can overwrite existing files without confirmation prompts!) Tj ET
0.600 0.100 0.100 rg
BT /F2 7.2 Tf 42.00 72.50 Td (5. VERIFY WITH PWD & LS: Always inspect directory contents with 'ls' before issuing batch wildcards \('rm *.log'\)!) Tj ET
